<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina auctions 182-, 91-day Letes T-bills.</title>
<headline>Argentina auctions 182-, 91-day Letes T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina Tuesday auctioned $250 million in 182-day Letes Treasury bills at a cut-off yield of 6.10 percent and 250 million pesos of 91-day bills at 6.0 percent, the Economy Ministry said.</p>
<p>There were 74 bids on the 182-day bills for a bid-to-cover ratio of 4.98 times and 82 bids for the 91-day bills for a bid-to-cover of 4.57 times.  </p>
<p>The price at the cut-off yield on the 182-day bills was 969.161 and on the 91-day bills 984.833.</p>
<p>Market-makers will be offered up to 10 percent more of both issues until 1700 local/2000 GMT.</p>
<p>Settlement is due May 16.</p>
<p>For more information see  ARG15 and  ARG16.</p>
<p>((--Axel Bugge, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0668))</p>
